#### Scenario 2: Extension Database Connection Leak

**Scenario**: Extension opens database connections but fails to dispose them properly.

**Test**:
```csharp
[Fact]
public async Task ConnectionLeak_DetectedAndContained()
{
    var testHost = new MultiTenantTestHost();
    var connectionMonitor = new ConnectionPoolMonitor();

    // Extension that leaks connections
    var leakyExtension = new ConnectionLeakingExtension();

    var initialAvailable = connectionMonitor.GetAvailableConnections();

    // Execute extension multiple times
    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)
    {
        await testHost.ExecuteExtensionAsync("TenantA", leakyExtension);
    }

    var afterExecutionAvailable = connectionMonitor.GetAvailableConnections();
    var leakedConnections = initialAvailable - afterExecutionAvailable;

    // Assert leak detected
    Assert.True(leakedConnections > 0, $"Leaked {leakedConnections} connections");

    // Verify monitoring triggered alert
    var alerts = testHost.GetResourceAlerts();
    Assert.Contains(alerts, a =>
        a.Type == AlertType.ConnectionLeak &&
        a.TenantId == "TenantA" &&
        a.ExtensionName == "ConnectionLeakingExtension");

    // Force cleanup
    await testHost.ForceConnectionCleanupAsync();

    var afterCleanupAvailable = connectionMonitor.GetAvailableConnections();
    Assert.True(afterCleanupAvailable > afterExecutionAvailable,
        "Cleanup should recover connections");
}

public class ConnectionLeakingExtension : IExtension
{
    public async Task<ExtensionResult> ExecuteAsync(ExtensionContext context)
    {
        // Open connection but don't dispose
        var connection = new SqlConnection(context.ConnectionString);
        await connection.OpenAsync();

        // LEAK: Connection never closed!

        return ExtensionResult.Success();
    }
}
```

**Expected Behavior**:
- Connection leak detected by monitoring
- Alert triggered after threshold exceeded
- Resource cleanup mechanism activated
- Leaked connections recovered
- Extension flagged for review
- Deployment blocked until fixed
